    <main class="doc-content">
      <!-- ═══ OVERVIEW ═══ -->
      <section id="overview" class="doc-section">
        <span class="doc-label">PROJECT</span>
        <h1 class="doc-h1">HandheldDB</h1>
        <p class="doc-intro">
          HandheldDB is a community-driven performance database for handheld gaming PCs. It answers one question:
          <strong>"Does this game run on my handheld?"</strong> — with real FPS data, optimal settings, and battery life estimates
          submitted by actual players.
        </p>

        <div class="doc-stats-grid">
          <div class="doc-stat-card">
            <span class="doc-stat-val">6,470</span>
            <span class="doc-stat-lbl">Games cataloged</span>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-stat-card">
            <span class="doc-stat-val">6</span>
            <span class="doc-stat-lbl">Active devices</span>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-stat-card">
            <span class="doc-stat-val">22</span>
            <span class="doc-stat-lbl">API endpoints</span>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-stat-card">
            <span class="doc-stat-val">20</span>
            <span class="doc-stat-lbl">Database tables</span>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-stat-card">
            <span class="doc-stat-val">16</span>
            <span class="doc-stat-lbl">React components</span>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-stat-card">
            <span class="doc-stat-val">11</span>
            <span class="doc-stat-lbl">Astro components</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="doc-h2">Core Features</h2>
        <div class="doc-feature-grid">
          <div class="doc-feature">
            <h3 class="doc-h3">Performance Reports</h3>
            <p>Users submit detailed performance reports: FPS averages, graphics presets, TDP settings, battery life, thermal behavior, and custom settings. Reports are voted on and aggregated into consensus ratings.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-feature">
            <h3 class="doc-h3">Consensus Ratings</h3>
            <p>A weighted algorithm processes all reports for a game+device pair into a single consensus: recommended settings, expected FPS, battery life, and an overall verdict (excellent/good/fair/poor/unplayable).</p>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-feature">
            <h3 class="doc-h3">Device Comparison</h3>
            <p>Side-by-side comparison of up to 3 handheld devices across specs and game performance. Battery estimator, FPS heatmaps, and shared game analysis.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-feature">
            <h3 class="doc-h3">Game Discovery</h3>
            <p>Browse 6,470+ games with filters by genre, Deck compatibility, Metacritic score, and search powered by Meilisearch with fuzzy matching.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-feature">
            <h3 class="doc-h3">Editorial Content</h3>
            <p>AI-assisted news articles covering game launches, patches, device updates, and performance analyses. RSS feed support and automated ingestion from gaming news sources.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="doc-feature">
            <h3 class="doc-h3">Community System</h3>
            <p>Threaded comments on game pages, report voting, game following, achievement badges, contributor leaderboard, and Steam library import.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="doc-h2">Supported Devices</h2>
        <table class="doc-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Device</th><th>Manufacturer</th><th>Chip</th><th>Battery</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Steam Deck (OLED)</td><td>Valve</td><td>AMD Van Gogh (custom APU)</td><td>50 Wh</td></tr>
            <tr><td>ROG Ally</td><td>ASUS</td><td>AMD Ryzen Z1 Extreme</td><td>40 Wh</td></tr>
            <tr><td>ROG Ally X</td><td>ASUS</td><td>AMD Ryzen Z1 Extreme</td><td>80 Wh</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Legion Go</td><td>Lenovo</td><td>AMD Ryzen Z1 Extreme</td><td>49.2 Wh</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Legion Go S</td><td>Lenovo</td><td>AMD Ryzen Z2 Go</td><td>55.5 Wh</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Claw 8 AI+</td><td>MSI</td><td>Intel Core Ultra 7 258V</td><td>80 Wh</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </section>

      <!-- ═══ ARCHITECTURE ═══ -->
      <section id="architecture" class="doc-section">
        <span class="doc-label">SYSTEM</span>
        <h1 class="doc-h1">Architecture</h1>

        <h2 class="doc-h2">High-Level Overview</h2>
        <div class="doc-code">
          <pre>┌──────────────────┐    ┌─────────────┐    ┌────────────────┐
│   Nginx (443)    │───▶│ Astro SSR   │───▶│   Supabase     │
│   SSL + Cache    │    │ (port 4321) │    │  (PostgreSQL)  │
└──────────────────┘    └─────────────┘    └────────────────┘
        │                      │                     │
   Static files          React Islands         Row-Level Security
   (/_astro/*)          (client:load)          Auth (JWT)
        │                      │                     │
   Proxy cache           Meilisearch            Drizzle ORM
   (5m TTL)             (full-text)            (migrations)</pre>
        </div>

        <h2 class="doc-h2">Request Flow</h2>
        <ol class="doc-list">
          <li><strong>Client</strong> hits <code>handhelddb.com</code> over HTTPS</li>
          <li><strong>Nginx</strong> terminates SSL, checks proxy cache. If cached → serve immediately</li>
          <li><strong>Astro SSR</strong> renders the page server-side, fetching data from Supabase</li>
          <li><strong>React islands</strong> hydrate on the client for interactive components (search, voting, forms)</li>
          <li><strong>API calls</strong> from React components hit <code>/api/*</code> endpoints, which query Supabase or Meilisearch</li>
          <li>Responses are proxy-cached by Nginx for subsequent visitors</li>
        </ol>

        <h2 class="doc-h2">Data Flow: Performance Report</h2>
        <ol class="doc-list">
          <li>User fills <code>ReportForm</code> at <code>/report/new</code></li>
          <li><code>POST /api/reports</code> validates and stores in <code>performance_reports</code></li>
          <li>Cron job (<code>cron-consensus.ts</code>) recalculates consensus ratings every 12h</li>
          <li>Consensus uses weighted median of all reports for that game+device</li>
          <li>Result stored in <code>consensus_ratings</code> with verdict, FPS, and recommended settings</li>
          <li>Game detail page fetches consensus data and renders it in real-time</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

